# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRangeDeleteWithoutIntent. A replicated or shadow-forwarded
# range delete, or a fan-out that began before the gate opened, reaches a shard
# root through an existing method that stamps it anyway. No marker holds L, so the
# stamped walk lies above the head L's marker reads.
MODULE: HandOffBoundRangeDeleteWithoutIntent
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a range-delete walk is stamped although no tree-fence intent is open
PERTURBS: GAdmit

--- FIND
    /\ WithTreeWalk
    /\ fAdmit
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst = "idle"
--- REPLACE
    /\ WithTreeWalk
\* MUTATION: stamped without an open intent; it should be appended unstamped.
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst = "idle"
--- END
